it == base+allowance\" while req_limit stays bare.","tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py:80 `assert limits.request_limit == 5` (with `assert eff_max_iter == 10`, max_iterations=10) — asserts on the built object, not the returned req_limit, so raising UsageLimits.request_limit to base+allowance breaks it."],"finding":"The plan changes build_usage_limits so the constructed UsageLimits.request_limit becomes base+allowance, but its affected-file inventory (test Scope) omits tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py, which asserts directly on the returned UsageLimits object — line 80: `assert limits.request_limit == 5` for max_iterations=10. That assertion breaks under the new behavior (5 becomes 5+OUTPUT_RETRIES=7), and the file is not in the plan's test Scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6f79295cd31eec88","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — tests: `tests/unit/test_structured_run.py, test_runner_pydantic_budget.py, test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`; and `build_usage_limits` cross-directory census","norm_id":"n50b41fb863510632","priority":0.85,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py::test_usage_limits_returns_the_limits_object_and_both_counters — line 80 `limits.request_limit == 5` now fails (value is 7), an unpatched/broken test not listed in Scope."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"List test_settings_builders_seam.py among the touched test files and adjust its line-80 assertion so it distinguishes UsageLimits.request_limit (base+allowance) from the returned req_limit (bare ceil(eff_max_iter/2)).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the provider_details truncation vocabulary the concision guard uses (which key(s)/values map to length/max_tokens truncation vs refusal/content_filter) so the reclassification split is deterministic on the raw-signal layer, not only the normalized finish_reason layer.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a truncation signal — in the normalized finish_reason (length/max_tokens) OR in raw response.provider_details — raises ... ModelRetry'","structured.py:632 _UNRETRYABLE_STOP_REASONS = frozenset({'refusal','max_tokens','length','content_filter'}) — truncation and refusal signals co-mingle in one set","structured.check_response reads details.get('finish_reason') against _UNRETRYABLE_STOP_REASONS AND 'refusal' in details (structured.py:672-676), so the provider_details layer carries BOTH truncation and refusal signals with no plan-named split for the guard's routing","Plan names the normalized truncation subset (length/max_tokens) but leaves the provider_details truncation subset unnamed"],"finding":"The concision guard's provider_details truncation-detection vocabulary is under-specified: the plan names normalized finish_reason truncation values (length/max_tokens) but does not name which provider_details keys/values count as truncation versus refusal, even though both truncation (length/max_tokens) and terminal (refusal/content_filter) signals share the one _UNRETRYABLE_STOP_REASONS frozenset that check_response consults.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fccde662c589c56b5","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (Truncation reclassification) / Scope pai_retry.py bullet (a)","norm_id":"n9818289298cf4c78","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A provider surfaces truncation only in provider_details (finish_reason None/stop) — the #5221 defense-in-depth shape check_response was built for — and the guard must choose concision-retry, not terminal","A refusal signal in provider_details must NOT be reclassified as concision-retryable"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Specify that the guard reads the same details.get('finish_reason') as check_response and treats raw values {length, max_tokens} as the truncation subset (-> concision ModelRetry) while all other _UNRETRYABLE_STOP_REASONS raw values and the 'refusal' key delegate to check_response's terminal path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","citation [rebar:grazeable-preferred-bumblebee] ('`_pai_structured` creates fresh Agent runs for prompted-output recovery, so outp') names no VERIFIED upstream prerequisite: P neither declares `depends_on -> grazeable-preferred-bumblebee` nor is blocked by it. Add a `depends_on` edge to grazeable-preferred-bumblebee, ensure grazeable-preferred-bumblebee `blocks` this ticket, or remove the citation. Until then the cited symbol is grounded as normal (fails closed)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ground how a ModelRetry raised from pai_retry's after_model_request capability is charged against pydantic-ai's retries={'output': allowance} budget (cite the accounting path), or state the concrete mechanism by which the concision retries and the output_function parse retries share one counter — so the shared-allowance and exhaustion ACs are demonstrably achievable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4284,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'Output-size (concision) and parse/validation retries draw from the SAME counter — structured.OUTPUT_RETRIES (=2) … not a separate budget.'","Plan step 2 raises the concision ModelRetry from pai_retry's own after_model_request capability, whereas the parse ModelRetry comes from pai_output.output_function (TextOutput fn).","pydantic-ai counts output-function ModelRetry against the retries={'output': N} budget (mirrored by the existing NativeOutput path at structured_run.py:128); whether a ModelRetry from an AbstractCapability.after_model_request hook is charged to that SAME 'output' budget (vs a general/tool retry counter, or uncounted) is unverified in the plan.","If the hook-raised concision ModelRetry does NOT share the 'output' counter, the exhaustion-translation and the 'consumes at most the configured output-retry allowance' AC break (concision retries could be unbounded or exhaustion never surfaces as UnexpectedModelBehavior)."],"finding":"The plan's 'one shared retry counter' invariant depends on a ModelRetry raised from the operation guard's after_model_request hook decrementing the SAME pydantic-ai OUTPUT retry budget as a ModelRetry raised from the output_function; this cross-seam counter-sharing is asserted but not grounded in pydantic-ai's retry-accounting semantics.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f613597a0fa02be02","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2/3 ('Truncation reclassification' + 'One shared request budget, one shared retry counter')","norm_id":"n26e7b43db43bc104","priority":0.1716,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Repeated length/max_tokens truncation drives concision retries; if those retries are charged to a different counter than parse retries, the shared-allowance and exhaustion contracts do not hold.","A tool turn + one parse retry + one concision retry: whether all three draw from one budget determines whether the 'succeeds at the derived allowance / fails one below it' limit test passes."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.65,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed"